QLModel","Datenbankmigrationen mit Alembic","Definition von Feldern mit spezifischen Datentypen","Verwendung von Indexen zur Leistungssteigerung der Datenbank","Erstellung von Datenmodellen mit Vererbung und Polymorphismus"],"pt":["Criação de padrões avançados de SQLModel","Migrações Alembic para bases de dados de produção","Definição de modelos de dados com Python","Utilização de campos indexados para melhorar a performance","Suporte a tipos de dados opcionais e não opcionais"],"ru":["Создание продвинутых шаблонов SQLModel","Миграции Alembic для баз данных производственного уровня","Определение моделей данных с помощью Python","Использование индексированных полей для улучшения производительности","Поддержка опциональных и неопциональных типов данных"],"ar":["إنشاء أنماط متقدمة من SQLModel","عمليات نقل Alembic للبيانات الإنتاجية","تعريف نماذج البيانات باستخدام Python","استخدام الحقول المؤشرة لتحسين الأداء","دعم أنواع البيانات الاختيارية والغير اختيارية"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use sqlmodel-expert","sqlmodel-expert alternative","sqlmodel-expert install","what is sqlmodel-expert","sqlmodel-expert vs Alembic","sqlmodel-expert setup guide","sqlmodel-expert python","sqlmodel-expert SQLModel patterns","sqlmodel-expert production databases"],"zh":["SQLModel Expert","AIエージェント","Python开发","数据库管理","Alembic迁移","SQLModel模式","生产数据库","数据模型定义"],"ja":["SQLModel Expert","AIエージェント","Python開発","データベース管理","Alembicマイグレーション","SQLModelパターン","生産性の高いデータベース","データモデル定義"],"ko":["SQLModel Expert","AI Tools","Python 개발","데이터베이스 관리","Alembic 마이그레이션","SQLModel 패턴","생산성 높은 데이터베이스","데이터 모델 정의"],"es":["SQLModel Expert","modelado de datos","migraciones de base de datos","Alembic","SQLModel","bases de datos de producción","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["SQLModel Expert","modélisation de données","migrations de base de données","Alembic","SQLModel","bases de données de production","développement de logiciels","outils de développement"],"de":["SQLModel Expert","Datenmodellierung","Datenbankmigrationen","Alembic","SQLModel","Produktionsdatenbanken","Softwareentwicklung","Entwicklungstools"],"pt":["SQLModel Expert","padrões avançados de SQLModel","migrações Alembic","bases de dados de produção","desenvolvimento de software","Python","SQLModel","Alembic"],"ru":["SQLModel Expert","продвинутые шаблоны SQLModel","миграции Alembic","базы данных производственного уровня","разработка программного обеспечения","Python","SQLModel","Alembic"],"ar":["SQLModel Expert","أنماط متقدمة من SQLModel","عمليات نقل Alembic","بيانات الإنتاجية","تطوير البرمجيات","Python","SQLModel","Alembic","أدوات البرمجة","تكنولوجيا المعلومات"]}},"owner":"JimScope","repo":"vendel","repoPath":"JimScope/vendel","stars":4,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-05T16:37:43Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"sqlmodel-expert","description":"Advanced SQLModel patterns and comprehensive database migrations with Alembic. Use when creating SQLModel models, defining relationships (one-to-many, many-to-many, self-referential), setting up database migrations, optimizing queries, solving N+1 problems, implementing inheritance patterns, working with composite keys, creating indexes, performing data migrations, or troubleshooting Alembic issues. Triggers include SQLModel, Alembic migration, database model, relationship, foreign key, migration, N+1 query, query optimization, database schema, or questions about ORM patterns.","bodyPreview":"# SQLModel Expert\n\nAdvanced SQLModel patterns and comprehensive Alembic migrations for production databases.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### Define a Basic Model\n\n```python\nfrom sqlmodel import Field, SQLModel\nfrom typing import Optional\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\nclass Task(SQLModel, table=True):\n    id: Optional[int] = Field(default=None, primary_key=True)\n    title: str = Field(index=True)\n    description: Optional[str] = None\n    completed: bool = Field(default=False)\n    created_at: datetime = Fie","body":"# SQLModel Expert\n\nAdvanced SQLModel patterns and comprehensive Alembic migrations for production databases.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### Define a Basic Model\n\n```python\nfrom sqlmodel import Field, SQLModel\nfrom typing import Optional\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\nclass Task(SQLModel, table=True):\n    id: Optional[int] = Field(default=None, primary_key=True)\n    title: str = Field(index=True)\n    description: Optional[str] = None\n    completed: bool = Field(default=False)\n    created_at: datetime = Field(default_factory=datetime.utcnow)\n```\n\n### Initialize Database\n\n```bash\n# Using provided script\npython scripts/init_db.py --url postgresql://user:pass@localhost/db\n\n# Or manually\nfrom sqlmodel import create_engine\nengine = create_engine(\"postgresql://user:pass@localhost/db\")\nSQLModel.metadata.create_all(engine)\n```\n\n### Create Migration\n\n```bash\n# Using provided helper script\n./scripts/migrate.sh create \"add user table\"\n\n# Or directly with Alembic\nalembic revision --autogenerate -m \"add user table\"\nalembic upgrade head\n```\n\n## Core Topics\n\n### 1. Advanced Model Patterns\n**See:** [references/advanced-models.md](references/advanced-models.md)\n\n- **Relationships**: One-to-many, many-to-many, self-referential\n- **Inheritance**: Single table, joined table, polymorphism\n- **Validation**: Pydantic validators, custom constraints\n- **Mixins**: Timestamp, soft delete, reusable patterns\n- **Field Types**: Enums, JSON, arrays, custom types\n- **Indexes**: Single, composite, partial indexes\n- **Constraints**: Unique, check, foreign key cascades\n\n### 2. Comprehensive Migrations\n**See:** [references/migrations.md](references/migrations.md)\n\n- **Alembic Setup**: Configuration, env.py for SQLModel\n- **Creating Migrations**: Autogenerate vs manual\n- **Schema Changes**: Add/drop columns, rename, change types\n- **Data Migrations**: Complex data transformations\n- **Production Workflow**: Zero-downtime migrations\n- **Rollback Strategies**: Safe downgrade patterns\n- **Troubleshooting**: Common issues and solutions\n\n### 3. Query Optimization\n**See:** [references/queries-optimization.md](references/queries-optimization.md)\n\n- **N+1 Problem**: Solutions with eager loading\n- **Query Patterns**: Joins, aggregations, subqueries\n- **Performance**: Indexes, batch operations, profiling\n- **Advanced Queries**: Window functions, CTEs\n- **Bulk Operations**: Insert, update, delete at scale\n- **Testing**: Query counting, explain analyze\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### One-to-Many Relationship\n\n```python\nfrom typing import List\nfrom sqlmodel import Field, Relationship, SQLModel\n\nclass Team(SQLModel, table=True):\n    id: Optional[int] = Field(default=None, primary_key=True)\n    name: str\n\n    # One team has many heroes\n    heroes: List[\"Hero\"] = Relationship(back_populates=\"team\")\n\nclass Hero(SQLModel, table=True):\n    id: Optional[int] = Field(default=None, primary_key=True)\n    name: str\n    team_id: Optional[int] = Field(foreign_key=\"team.id\")\n\n    # Many heroes belong to one team\n    team: Optional[Team] = Relationship(back_populates=\"heroes\")\n```\n\n### Many-to-Many with Link Table\n\n```python\nclass HeroTeamLink(SQLModel, table=True):\n    hero_id: int = Field(foreign_key=\"hero.id\", primary_key=True)\n    team_id: int = Field(foreign_key=\"team.id\", primary_key=True)\n    joined_at: datetime = Field(default_factory=datetime.utcnow)\n\nclass Hero(SQLModel, table=True):\n    id: Optional[int] = Field(default=None, primary_key=True)\n    name: str\n    teams: List[\"Team\"] = Relationship(\n        back_populates=\"heroes\",\n        link_model=HeroTeamLink\n    )\n\nclass Team(SQLModel, table=True):\n    id: Optional[int] = Field(default=None, primary_key=True)\n    name: str\n    heroes: List[Hero] = Relationship(\n        back_populates=\"teams\",\n        link_model=HeroTeamLink\n    )\n```\n\n### Solving N+1 Query Problem\n\n```python\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import selectinload\n\n# BAD - N+1 queries\nusers = session.exec(select(User)).all()\nfor user in users:\n    posts = user.posts  # Each triggers a query!\n\n# GOOD - Eager loading (2 queries total)\nstatement = select(User).options(selectinload(User.posts))\nusers = session.exec(statement).all()\nfor user in users:\n    posts = user.posts  # No additional query!\n```\n\n### Creating a Migration\n\n```python\n# 1. Modify your model\nclass User(SQLModel, table=True):\n    id: Optional[int] = Field(default=None, primary_key=True)\n    email: str\n    phone: str  # New field added\n\n# 2. Generate migration\n# alembic revision --autogenerate -m \"add phone to user\"\n\n# 3. Review generated migration\ndef upgrade() -> None:\n    op.add_column(''user'', sa.Column(''phone'', sa.String(), nullable=True))\n\ndef downgrade() -> None:\n    op.drop_column(''user'', ''phone'')\n\n# 4. Apply migration\n# alembic upgrade head\n```\n\n## Migration Helper Scripts\n\n### Initialize Database\n```bash\npython scripts/init_db.py --url postgresql://user:pass@localhost/db\n```\n\n### Migration Operations\n```bash\n./scripts/migrate.sh init              # Initialize Alembic\n./scripts/migrate.sh create \"message\"  # Create migration\n./scripts/migrate.sh upgrade           # Apply migrations\n./scripts/migrate.sh downgrade         # Rollback one\n./scripts/migrate.sh current           # Show current\n./scripts/migrate.sh history           # Show history\n./scripts/migrate.sh test              # Test up & down\n```\n\n## Example Models\n\nUse the example models in `assets/example-models.py` as templates:\n\n- User model with timestamp mixin\n- Task model with enums and relationships\n- Team model with many-to-many\n- Tag system with link tables\n- Separate read/write/update models\n\nCopy to your project:\n```bash\ncp assets/example-models.py your-project/app/models.py\n```\n\n## Best Practices Checklist\n\n### Model Design\n- [ ] Use type hints for all fields\n- [ ] Separate read/write/update models\n- [ ] Use mixins for common fields (timestamps, soft delete)\n- [ ] Define indexes on foreign keys and frequently queried columns\n- [ ] Use enums for constrained choices\n- [ ] Implement proper validation with Pydantic validators\n\n### Relationships\n- [ ] Use `back_populates` for bidirectional relationships\n- [ ] Create explicit link tables for many-to-many\n- [ ] Consider cascade delete behavior\n- [ ] Use eager loading to prevent N+1 queries\n- [ ] Index foreign key columns\n\n### Migrations\n- [ ] Always review autogenerated migrations\n- [ ] One logical change per migration\n- [ ] Test both upgrade and downgrade\n- [ ] Use descriptive migration names\n- [ ] Never edit applied migrations\n- [ ] Add data migrations when changing schemas\n- [ ] Backup database before production migrations\n\n### Query Optimization\n- [ ] Use eager loading (selectinload) for relationships\n- [ ] Select only needed columns\n- [ ] Use indexes for WHERE/ORDER BY columns\n- [ ] Batch operations instead of loops\n- [ ] Profile slow queries\n- [ ] Use connection pooling\n\n## Troubleshooting Guide\n\n### Migration Issues\n\n**Problem**: Alembic doesn''t detect model changes\n```python\n# Solution: Ensure models are imported in env.py\nfrom app.models import User, Task, Team  # Import all models\ntarget_metadata = SQLModel.metadata\n```\n\n**Problem**: Failed migration\n```bash\n# Check current state\nalembic current\n\n# Manually fix issue, then stamp\nalembic stamp head\n\n# Or downgrade and retry\nalembic downgrade -1\nalembic upgrade head\n```\n\n### Query Performance\n\n**Problem**: Slow queries\n```python\n# Enable query logging\nlogging.getLogger(''sqlalchemy.engine'').setLevel(logging.INFO)\n\n# Use EXPLAIN ANALYZE\nexplain = session.exec(text(\"EXPLAIN ANALYZE SELECT ...\")).all()\n\n# Profile queries\n# See references/queries-optimization.md for detailed patterns\n```\n\n**Problem**: N+1 queries\n```python\n# Use selectinload\nstatement = select(User).options(selectinload(User.posts))\n\n# Or joinedload\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import joinedload\nstatement = select(User).options(joinedload(User.posts))\n```\n\n## Production Workflow\n\n### Development\n1. Modify SQLModel models\n2. Generate migration: `./scripts/migrate.sh create \"description\"`\n3. Review generated migration file\n4. Test migration: `./scripts/migrate.sh test`\n5. Commit migration file\n\n### Staging\n1. Deploy application code\n2. Run migrations: `alembic upgrade head`\n3. Verify data integrity\n4. Test application\n\n### Production\n1. Backup database: `pg_dump mydb > backup.sql`\n2. Deploy in maintenance window\n3. Run migrations: `alembic upgrade head`\n4. Monitor logs and metrics\n5. Verify application functionality\n\n## Zero-Downtime Migration Strategy\n\nFor large production databases:\n\n```python\n# Phase 1: Add new column (nullable)\ndef upgrade():\n    op.add_column(''user'', sa.Column(''new_email'', sa.String(), nullable=True))\n\n# Deploy app version that writes to both columns\n\n# Phase 2: Backfill data\ndef upgrade():\n    op.execute(\"UPDATE user SET new_email = email WHERE new_email IS NULL\")\n\n# Phase 3: Make non-nullable\ndef upgrade():\n    op.alter_column(''user'', ''new_email'', nullable=False)\n\n# Deploy app version that reads from new column\n\n# Phase 4: Drop old column\ndef upgrade():\n    op.drop_column(''user'', ''email'')\n```\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n- **Advanced Patterns**: See references/advanced-models.md for inheritance, polymorphism, composite keys\n- **Migration Guide**: See references/migrations.md for Alembic mastery\n- **Query Optimization**: See references/queries-optimization.md for performance tuning\n\nThis skill provides everything needed for professional SQLModel development and database management.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-06T06:59:31.408Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Python Analysis Agents needing advanced SQLModel patterns and Alembic migrations for production databases.","zh":"非常适合需要高级 SQLModel 模式和 Alembic 迁移的 Python 分析代理，用于生产数据库。","ja":"Python 分析エージェントが高度な SQLModel パターンと Alembic 移行を必要とする場合に最適です。生産用データベースで使用します。","ko":"고급 SQLModel 패턴과 Alembic 마이그레이션이 필요한 Python 분석 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 프로덕션 데이터베이스에서 사용합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Análisis de Python que necesitan patrones de SQLModel avanzados y migraciones de Alembic para bases de datos de producción.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse Python nécessitant des modèles de SQLModel avancés et des migrations Alembic pour les bases de données de production.","de":"Perfekt für Python-Analyseagenten, die erweiterte SQLModel-Muster und Alembic-Migrationen für Produktionsdatenbanken benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise Python que necessitam de padrões SQLModel avançados e migrações Alembic para bancos de dados de produção.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа Python, которым требуются продвинутые шаблоны SQLModel и миграции Alembic для производственных баз данных.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل Python الذي يحتاج إلى نمط SQLModel متقدم وترحيل Alembic لقواعد البيانات الإنتاجية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to define complex SQLModel patterns, leverage comprehensive Alembic migrations, and interact with production databases using Python and SQLModel, streamlining database operations and migrations.","zh":"赋予代理定义复杂的 SQLModel 模式、利用全面 Alembic 迁移，并使用 Python 和 SQLModel 与生产数据库交互，简化数据库操作和迁移。","ja":"エージェントが複雑な SQLModel パターンを定義し、包括的な Alembic 移行を利用し、Python と SQLModel を使用して生産用データベースとやり取りすることで、データベース操作と移行を스트リーミングします。","ko":"에이전트가 복잡한 SQLModel 패턴을 정의하고, 포괄적인 Alembic 마이그레이션을 활용하며, Python 및 SQLModel을 사용하여 프로덕션 데이터베이스와 상호 작용할 수 있도록 하여 데이터베이스 운영 및 마이그레이션을 간소화합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a definir patrones de SQLModel complejos, aprovechar migraciones de Alembic completas y interactuar con bases de datos de producción utilizando Python y SQLModel, simplificando las operaciones y migraciones de bases de datos.","fr":"Permet aux agents de définir des modèles de SQLModel complexes, d''utiliser des migrations Alembic complètes et d''interagir avec les bases de données de production à l''aide de Python et de SQLModel, rationalisant ainsi les opérations et les migrations de bases de données.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, komplexe SQLModel-Muster zu definieren, umfassende Alembic-Migrationen zu nutzen und mit Produktionsdatenbanken mithilfe von Python und SQLModel zu interagieren, wodurch Datenbankoperationen und -migrationen rationalisiert werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a definir padrões SQLModel complexos, aproveitar migrações Alembic abrangentes e interagir com bancos de dados de produção usando Python e SQLModel, simplificando as operações e migrações de banco de dados.","ru":"Позволяет агентам определять сложные шаблоны SQLModel, использовать полные миграции Alembic и взаимодействовать с производственными базами данных с помощью Python и SQLModel, оптимизируя операции с базами данных и миграции.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل تحديد أنماط SQLModel المعقدة وتحقيق ترحيل Alembic الشامل والتفاعل مع قواعد البيانات الإنتاجية باستخدام Python و SQLModel ، مما يُبسط عمليات قاعدة البيانات والترحيل."},"useCases":{"en":["Defining advanced SQLModel patterns for production databases","Generating comprehensive Alembic migrations for database schema updates","Automating database interactions using Python and SQLModel"],"zh":["为生产数据库定义高级 SQLModel 模式","为数据库模式更新生成全面 Alembic 迁移","使用 Python 和 SQLModel 自动执行数据库交互"],"ja":["生産用データベースのための高度な SQLModel パターンの定義","データベース スキーマの更新のための包括的な Alembic 移行の生成","Python と SQLModel を使用したデータベースのやり取りの自動化"],"ko":["프로덕션 데이터베이스를 위한 고급 SQLModel 패턴 정의","데이터베이스 스키마 업데이트를 위한 포괄적인 Alembic 마이그레이션 생성","Python 및 SQLModel을 사용한 데이터베이스 상호 작용 자동화"],"es":["Definir patrones de SQLModel avanzados para bases de datos de producción","Generar migraciones de Alembic completas para actualizaciones del esquema de base de datos","Automatizar las interacciones de base de datos utilizando Python y SQLModel"],"fr":["Définir des modèles de SQLModel avancés pour les bases de données de production","Générer des migrations Alembic complètes pour les mises à jour du schéma de base de données","Automatiser les interactions de base de données à l''aide de Python et de SQLModel"],"de":["Erweiterte SQLModel-Muster für Produktionsdatenbanken definieren","Umfassende Alembic-Migrationen für Datenbankschemataktualisierungen generieren","Datenbankinteraktionen mit Python und SQLModel automatisieren"],"pt":["Definir padrões SQLModel avançados para bancos de dados de produção","Gerar migrações Alembic abrangentes para atualizações de esquema de banco de dados","Automatizar interações de banco de dados usando Python e SQLModel"],"ru":["Определение продвинутых шаблонов SQLModel для производственных баз данных","Генерация полных миграций Alembic для обновлений схемы базы данных","Автоматизация взаимодействия с базами данных с помощью Python и SQLModel"],"ar":["تحديد أنماط SQLModel المتقدمة لقواعد البيانات الإنتاجية","توليد ترحيل Alembic الشامل لتحديث مخطط قاعدة البيانات","تأتمتة التفاعل مع قواعد البيانات باستخدام Python و SQLModel"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python and SQLModel installation","Alembic migration dependencies"],"zh":["需要 Python 和 SQLModel 安装","Alembic 迁移依赖"],"ja":["Python と SQLModel のインストールが必要","Alembic 移行の依存関係"],"ko":["Python 및 SQLModel 설치 필요","Alembic 마이그레이션 종속성"],"es":["Requiere la instalación de Python y SQLModel","Dependencias de migración de Alembic"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de Python et de SQLModel","Dépendances de migration Alembic"],"de":["Benötigt die Installation von Python und SQLModel","Alembic-Migrationsabhängigkeiten"],"pt":["Requer instalação do Python e SQLModel","Dependências de migração Alembic"],"ru":["Требует установки Python и SQLModel","Зависимости миграции Alembic"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت Python و SQLModel","اعتماديات ترحيل Alembic"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"4c1b3b67958c4b955390798c98278f482f9569a6f2608023654ef065950e57ab","qualityScore":36}');
